# TestJavaToCSharpLangchain4jFacts: langchain4j-core printed as C# with the modification analysis's and the
# NullabilityPass's facts (Policy.KOTLIN), judged by Roslyn (see maddi-run-openjdk's JavaToCSharpRatchet). Lower is
# better for printerCrashes, syntaxErrors, unmappedJdkUses and nullableWarnings, higher for syntaxCleanFiles and
# compilingFiles; `types` must not move. Write a better value here in the commit that earns it.
#
# 2026-10-12, first record, with maddi 369d81117: the same 271 compiling files, 154 unmapped JDK uses and 232 errors as
# maddi's langchain4j.ratchet without the analysis. 100 nullable warnings (250 before that maddi commit, whose
# EnsureNotNull<T>(T? o) took 69 of 75 CS8601 and 72 of 85 CS8618 of the validation idiom this = EnsureNotNull(x, "x")).
#
# 2026-10-12, nullable library results (object.ToString(), node[k], reflection), ? on class type parameters, (T?) null,
# = null! where C# cannot see the assignment (maddi 3a4a1daf9): 100 -> 54 nullable warnings, CS8602 16 -> 7, CS8603 16
# -> 6, CS8618 13 -> 4, CS8622 6 -> 0, CS8600 8 -> 2.
#
# 2026-10-12, maddi's printer for timefold (maddi 94fd25386: companions of self-bounded types, inner classes,
# explicit type arguments, …): 271 -> 284 compiling files, 54 -> 53 nullable warnings.
#
# 2026-10-12, after the merged nullability work and maddi e15baf22f (result-only self-bounded type parameters
# erased): 53 -> 52 nullable warnings.
#
# 2026-10-13, maddi ff94c0d60: the JDK mappings that came with JAXB: 154 -> 153 unmapped uses.
#
# 2026-10-13, maddi c2be5f33e: a type parameter that is, or is passed as, a dictionary's key is where K : notnull
# (CS8714): 52 -> 49 nullable warnings.
#
# 2026-10-13, maddi ce6ecea39: notnull dictionary keys through wildcards (CS8714 4 -> 1), measured together with
# the JDK nullability hints from JSpecify's annotated JDK (fd3f8419c, merged in the meantime), which move the
# printer's ! assertions throughout: 49 -> 55 nullable warnings.
types	346
printerCrashes	0
syntaxErrors	0
